From 1490f9e428fcf5133e311382ebf37d0853629638 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:56:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 81/94] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm630: Switch the NoCs to two
 interconnect cells

The SMD RPM interconnect providers take a second cell carrying the
RPM context tag (RPM_ACTIVE_TAG / RPM_SLEEP_TAG / RPM_ALWAYS_TAG),
and the one-cell form is deprecated in qcom,rpm-common.yaml. Without
the tag cell there is no way for a consumer to ask for an active-only
vote, which the CPU bandwidth monitor needs: its vote must go away
while the application processor is in power collapse, or it holds
DDR up in the RPM sleep set.

Move all six SDM630/SDM660 NoCs to #interconnect-cells = <2> and give
every existing path RPM_ALWAYS_TAG. icc-rpm already treats a zero tag
as RPM_ALWAYS_TAG, so these paths vote exactly as before. The
sdm660-hiby-rs6 board path to the hm100 SPI controller is converted
in the same commit, since a one-cell specifier no longer parses.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
